# NOTE: API keys are intentionally NOT set here or anywhere in the frontend.
# Anything prefixed VITE_ gets bundled into the client and is visible to users.
#
# Production keys live server-side in the Vercel serverless functions (/api):
#   - Set YOUTUBE_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY in Vercel → Project → Settings →
#     Environment Variables (or in a repo-root .env when running `vercel dev`).
#
# For local development with plain `npm run dev` (no /api available), enter
# keys via the in-app Settings modal instead — they stay in your browser only.

# Supabase project config — these ARE safe client-side: the anon key is public
# by design, and Row-Level Security (see supabase/schema.sql) is what actually
# enforces per-user data isolation, not secrecy of this key.
#
# If both are unset, the app runs in local/unauthenticated mode: no login
# screen, analyses stored in browser localStorage only (today's behavior).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# Early-access waitlist (apply + admin approve). Off by default.
# VITE_WAITLIST_ENABLED=true
